{"type":"standard","title":"Eugene Vindman","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Eugene Vindman</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q112610369","titles":{"canonical":"Eugene_Vindman","normalized":"Eugene Vindman","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Eugene Vindman</span></span>"},"pageid":63052780,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Representative_Eugene_Vindman_Official_Portrait.jpg/330px-Representative_Eugene_Vindman_Official_Portrait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":413},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b0/Representative_Eugene_Vindman_Official_Portrait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":3360,"height":4200},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1377358862","tid":"1fa676e9-bbab-11f1-94dd-1e96381b22b2","timestamp":"2026-09-29T02:11:47Z","description":"American military officer and politician (born 1975)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eugene_Vindman","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eugene_Vindman?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eugene_Vindman?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Eugene_Vindman"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eugene_Vindman","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Eugene_Vindman","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eugene_Vindman?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Eugene_Vindman"}},"extract":"Eugene Semyon Vindman is an American politician, lawyer, and retired U.S. Army officer serving as the U.S. representative for Virginia's 7th congressional district since 2025. A member of the Democratic Party, he was a deputy legal advisor for the United States National Security Council (NSC) until he was reassigned on February 7, 2020.","extract_html":"<p><b>Eugene Semyon Vindman</b> is an American politician, lawyer, and retired U.S. Army officer serving as the U.S. representative for Virginia's 7th congressional district since 2025. A member of the Democratic Party, he was a deputy legal advisor for the United States National Security Council (NSC) until he was reassigned on February 7, 2020.</p>"}